er/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sec x+\\tan x+2\\sin x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721528} {:answer/id #uuid "c835d3d7-48a2-5db9-bc97-3c1afad459b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sec x+\\sec x+2\\sin x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721532} {:answer/id #uuid "f0fb61f7-ca79-5d21-9e56-a367c0fd1387" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sec x\\tan x+\\tan x+2\\sin x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721539}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "662770a6-dab0-5f66-880f-461f41a1de90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3\\sec x+\\tan x+2\\sin x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721519} :answer-field/id #uuid "c4c3936a-134e-52b5-b574-73d600ff9331" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721529}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "7cd8e26a-2e37-50c8-8760-a1a02cc08cfd" :question/problem "Calculate\n$$\n\\int \\left(\\sec x\\left(-3\\tan x+\\sec x\\right)+2\\cos x\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x.\n$$\n" :question/worked-solution "Recall that\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int \\sec x\\tan x\\,\\mathrm{d}x&=\\sec x+C. \\\\\n\\int \\sec^2 x\\,\\mathrm{d}x&=\\tan x+C. \\\\\n\\int \\cos x\\,\\mathrm{d}x&=\\sin x+C.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nDistribute the secant factor:\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&\\left(\\sec x\\left(-3\\tan x+\\sec x\\right)+2\\cos x\\right) \\\\\n&=-3\\sec x\\tan x+\\sec^2 x+2\\cos x.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nApply the sum and constant factor rules, then collect the signs:\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&\\int \\left(\\sec x\\left(-3\\tan x+\\sec x\\right)+2\\cos x\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\\n&=-3\\int \\sec x\\tan x\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\\n&\\quad+\\int \\sec^2 x\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\\n&\\quad+2\\int \\cos x\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\\n&=-3\\left(\\sec x\\right)+\\left(\\tan x\\right)+2\\left(\\sin x\\right)+C \\\\\n&=-3\\sec x+\\tan x+2\\sin x+C.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nOne arbitrary constant suffices for the combined antiderivative."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186724749 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f3249b9-94c8-5dd8-ba25-8713699dd2e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186724751} {:answer/id #uuid "4b7e8269-967f-50aa-9c84-890bb88b0bf9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186724754}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3f3249b9-94c8-5dd8-ba25-8713699dd2e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186724751} :answer-field/id #uuid "0fb604a2-af0d-5ef2-b997-b4d1e0fc2573" :answer-field/key "At every point $(x,y)$ where $x<1$ and $y<-1$, the slope of the slope field is negative." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186724744} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "58652e79-b29f-527e-a32d-8628101ba984" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186724757} {:answer/id #uuid "7d83e0a2-0f8a-5b34-b4a6-40a8a73292c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186724764}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7d83e0a2-0f8a-5b34-b4a6-40a8a73292c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186724764} :answer-field/id #uuid "1b934f77-fdf2-53df-bbe4-25744dc57200" :answer-field/key "At every point $(x,y)$ where $x>1$ and $y<-1$, the slope of the slope field is positive." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186724746} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6d090ae9-d8f8-5eb2-b0a8-cef36096b9e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186724760} {:answer/id #uuid "8d6ebe1a-3a9c-57f0-8d40-831e390d9178" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186724767}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8d6ebe1a-3a9c-57f0-8d40-831e390d9178" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186724767} :answer-field/id #uuid "7891c483-9af5-56af-886f-d22d37268664" :answer-field/key "At every point $(x,y)$ where $x<1$ and $y>-1$, the slope of the slope field is positive." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186724763}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "266b2e33-e9d7-5ab2-b786-9256a0021c24" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation $\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=(x-1)(y+1)^2$ and its slope field. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x,y)=(x-1)(y+1)^2$. The slope is zero exactly when $x=1$ or $y=-1$.\n\n![The lines x equals 1 and y equals minus 1 divide the plane into four open regions.](images/62/62095f39261e489d0990ef866bf83531942bceb65577f90ce6756cb4aa7d8794.png)\n\nFor $y\\ne-1$, the squared factor $(y+1)^2$ is strictly positive on both sides of $y=-1$. Crossing that line does not reverse the sign. Thus, in each open region, the slope has the sign of $x-1$.\n\n| Region | $x-1$ | $(y+1)^2$ | $f(x,y)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x<1$, $y>-1$ | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n| $x>1$, $y>-1$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| $x<1$, $y<-1$ | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n| $x>1$, $y<-1$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n\n![Slopes are negative in both regions left of x equals 1 and positive in both regions right of x equals 1.](images/9a/9a8e625896128a39b4b04620c51ea318a6e351aa74bcb884455cac7b6ca3bb12.png)\n\n- For $x<1$ and $y>-1$, the slope is negative, so the first statement is false.\n- For $x<1$ and $y<-1$, the slope is still negative: squaring the negative quantity $y+1$ makes it positive. The second statement is true.\n- For $x>1$ and $y<-1$, both $x-1$ and $(y+1)^2$ are positive. The third statement is true.\n\nSelect the second and third statements. The squared factor is zero on $y=-1$, not positive there; the strict inequalities exclude that line."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186724756 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cb9ef9a0-6eb3-5450-af71-fe220f7be8fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186724769} {:answer/id #uuid "db6e300f-5475-5175-b29d-1ac21559e6c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186724771}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "db6e300f-5475-5175-b29d-1ac21559e6c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186724771} :answer-field/id #uuid "14c429c4-7264-5669-9cd4-653cd273197f" :answer-field/key "At every point $(x,y)$ where $x>1$ and $y>-1$, the slope of the slope field is positive." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186724745} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "63f54011-f122-53df-951f-0ef53079e168" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186724759} {:answer/id #uuid "823425ba-0638-50d4-b35e-17386003602e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186724765}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "63f54011-f122-53df-951f-0ef53079e168" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186724759} :answer-field/id #uuid "23a6a4eb-775b-5ac8-afae-53a596759712" :answer-field/key "At every point $(x,y)$ where $x<1$ and $y<-1$, the slope of the slope field is negative." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186724748} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8cdeed9d-77d5-5403-a989-9e90797b1f44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186724766} {:answer/id #uuid "ed9d738d-6434-5009-90ab-1345995433ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186724773}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ed9d738d-6434-5009-90ab-1345995433ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186724773} :answer-field/id #uuid "a9850f5d-5fac-5784-ada7-1c67d16c4170" :answer-field/key "At every point $(x,y)$ where $x<1$ and $y>-1$, the slope of the slope field is negative." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186724768}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "54a5f4e4-c288-5b50-9298-907a1f780b2b" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation $\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=(x-1)(y+1)$ and its slope field.\n\nThe zero-slope lines are $x=1$ and $y=-1$, shown below. Use the signs of the two factors in each region.\n\n![The lines x equals 1 and y equals minus 1 divide the plane into four open regions.](images/62/62095f39261e489d0990ef866bf83531942bceb65577f90ce6756cb4aa7d8794.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true? Select all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x,y)=(x-1)(y+1)$. The slope at $(x,y)$ is $f(x,y)$.\n\nOn the lines $x=1$ or $y=-1$, a factor is zero, so the slope is zero. Away from these lines, each factor has a fixed sign in each open region. Multiplying those signs gives:\n\n| Region | $x-1$ | $y+1$ | $f(x,y)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x<1$, $y>-1$ | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n| $x>1$, $y>-1$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| $x<1$, $y<-1$ | $-$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n| $x>1$, $y<-1$ | $+$ | $-$ | $-$ |\n\n![Positive slopes in the top-right and bottom-left regions; negative slopes in the other two regions.](images/bd/bd579831f075daa214856741018e525aac006d47a64367f5cbec804493f19019.png)\n\n- For $x>1$ and $y>-1$, both factors are positive. The first statement is true.\n- For $x<1$ and $y<-1$, both factors are negative, so their product is positive. The second statement, which claims a negative slope, is false.\n- For $x<1$ and $y>-1$, the factors have opposite signs. The third statement is true.\n\nSelect the first and third statements. The strict inequalities exclude the zero-slope lines."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186724761 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46c21d9d-a7a8-54bf-97c6-9be251b9b9f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186724752} {:answer/id #uuid "5df0cec2-f41f-590a-a213-0535aaf6917d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186724758}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5df0cec2-f41f-590a-a213-0535aaf6917d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186724758} :answer-field/id #uuid "1e194ed6-a85d-5754-b22d-725cb3258eaa" :answer-field/key "At every point $(x,y)$ where $x>1$ and $y>-1$, the slope of the slope field is positive." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186724747} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "78058c04-fd55-525f-841b-36d0e4c87d8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186724762} {:answer/id #uuid "e273b377-45d4-5d32-b663-fcbb7411c06e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186724772}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e273b377-45d4-5d32-b663-fcbb7411c06e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186724772} :answer-field/id #uuid "31bd9662-e056-5610-932e-5cd1b6bf77ed" :answer-field/key "At every point $(x,y)$ where $x>1$ and $y<-1$, the slope of the slope field is positive." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186724750} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "495022ec-f21d-5035-8755-5a219cd84f8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186724753} {:answer/id #uuid "d143a6b4-8911-5191-aa85-c80fffacbcb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186724770}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d143a6b4-8911-5191-aa85-c80fffacbcb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186724770} :answer-field/id #uuid "5439b81b-a4ab-5344-b815-cd04856b1c6e" :answer-field/key "At every point $(x,y)$ where $x<1$ and $y>-1$, the slope of the slope field is negative." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186724755}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "6f717802-9cc0-5e44-a0b1-4fe35c31f23c" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation $\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=(1-x)(y+1)$ and its slope field. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x,y)=(1-x)(y+1)$. The slope is zero exactly when $x=1$ or $y=-1$. These lines divide the plane into four open regions.\n\n![The lines x equals 1 and y equals minus 1 divide the plane into four open regions.](images/62/62095f39261e489d0990ef866bf83531942bceb65577f90ce6756cb4aa7d8794.png)\n\nThe factor $1-x$ is positive when $x<1$ and negative when $x>1$. The factor $y+1$ is positive above $y=-1$ and negative below it. Neither factor changes sign inside one of these regions.\n\n| Region | $1-x$ | $y+1$ | $f(x,y)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x<1$, $y>-1$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| $x>1$, $y>-1$ | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n| $x<1$, $y<-1$ | $+$ | $-$ | $-$ |\n| $x>1$, $y<-1$ | $-$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n\n![Positive slopes in the top-left and bottom-right regions; negative slopes in the other two regions.](images/7d/7ddf4fb413d0ddc61b5c1071ee299c0f8069c06d455e2598cf3ebc9bd8282a27.png)\n\n- For $x>1$ and $y>-1$, the slope is negative, so the first statement is false.\n- For $x>1$ and $y<-1$, both factors are negative and the slope is positive, so the second statement is true.\n- For $x<1$ and $y>-1$, both factors are positive and the slope is positive, so the third statement is false.\n\nSelect only the second statement. On either dividing line the slope is zero; those lines are excluded by the strict inequalities."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186724977 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "177b8449-bd8b-5be0-80f4-14352bb7ad08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186724979} {:answer/id #uuid "f44d53e9-307e-57d6-b2a3-3df09851ea49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725034}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f44d53e9-307e-57d6-b2a3-3df09851ea49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725034} :answer-field/id #uuid "72b2