45487} :question/id #uuid "52c0b320-ba9b-5c98-8a4f-767110cc222b" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{dy}{dx}=(x+1)(1-y)$ and its slope field.\n\nWhich of the following statements are true? Select all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x,y)=(x+1)(1-y)$. The slope at $(x,y)$ is $f(x,y)$. A factor is zero on $x=-1$ or $y=1$, so these are the zero-slope lines.\n\n![Zero-slope lines dividing the plane into four open regions.](images/20/2014f8cf31de0757d1a40d847dafcf51459c069faa88ffc30270b6fa1c041b00.png)\n\nAway from these lines, each factor has a fixed sign throughout each open region. Multiply the factor signs to determine the slope sign.\n\n| Region | $(x+1)$ | $(1-y)$ | $f(x,y)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x<-1$, $y>1$ | $-$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n| $x>-1$, $y>1$ | $+$ | $-$ | $-$ |\n| $x<-1$, $y<1$ | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n| $x>-1$, $y<1$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n\n![Signs of the slope in all four open regions.](images/1c/1cd588d10ecdbc0eb4ecce68a338fa0e6d32b45318d5605c16e6cb6555d5bdd3.png)\n\n- Statement 1: for $x<-1$ and $y>1$, the slope is positive. The statement is **true**.\n- Statement 2: for $x<-1$ and $y<1$, the slope is negative. The statement is **true**.\n- Statement 3: for $x>-1$ and $y<1$, the slope is positive. The statement is **true**.\n\n“None of the above” is **false** because at least one ordinary statement is true.\n\nThe strict inequalities exclude the zero-slope lines; the slope is zero on those lines."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725002 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c1906e08-e3bc-5121-b9a8-31d11659bbaf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725019} {:answer/id #uuid "eb389644-a9e0-586e-abc1-9ae6c7acdddc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725031}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eb389644-a9e0-586e-abc1-9ae6c