slope in all four open regions.](images/1a/1a177a1467ca3b6d51c28974a47327f531d61828b0b0d36bc69d757699877693.png)\n\n- Statement 1: for $x>2$ and $y<1$, the slope is positive. The statement is **false**.\n- Statement 2: for $x<2$ and $y<1$, the slope is negative. The statement is **true**.\n- Statement 3: for $x>2$ and $y>1$, the slope is negative. The statement is **false**.\n\n“None of the above” is **false** because at least one ordinary statement is true.\n\nThe strict inequalities exclude the zero-slope lines; the slope is zero on those lines."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725007 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "84226ee1-6de4-536e-b7df-5abec1600c80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186724999} {:answer/id #uuid "929735d8-fa99-542a-b51a-e52fd7a0aa13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725008}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "84226ee1-6de4-536e-b7df-5abec1600c80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186724999} :answer-field/id #uuid "54b03512-2c32-5454-befe-5429dc383dec" :answer-field/key "At every point $(x,y)$ where $x>-3$ and $y<2$, the slope of the slope field is positive." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186724989} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "74387e03-9a19-5ab7-b6e5-6a52e83aa81d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186724995} {:answer/id #uuid "8dcb088b-43f0-55f5-92c9-f63cdb01b6fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725005}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8dcb088b-43f0-55f5-92c9-f63cdb01b6fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725005} :answer-field/id #uuid "894b215b-39a0-599c-a03f-2f453e64c429" :answer-field/key "At every point $(x,y)$ where $x>-3$ and $y>2$, the slope of the slope field is negative." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725004} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4b6f7561-5175-510b-8ffb-ad87fabc849e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186724985} {:answer/id #uuid "7e412b3b-17d7-5e41-90d8-80e7453142d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186724998}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4b6f7561-5175-510b-8ffb-ad87fabc849e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186724985} :answer-field/id #uuid "c7201943-9a32-5d7f-b3ee-7c3d981f4a41" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725020} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4843e707-9c5a-5aa6-b196-0063b0ac2c5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186724984} {:answer/id #uuid "79e8746c-663a-557e-a053-c14cd30515b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186724997}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4843e707-9c5a-5aa6-b196-0063b0ac2c5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186724984} :answer-field/id #uuid "e4918685-bb20-5a00-8b9e-fd38928bdc9f" :answer-field/key "At every point $(x,y)$ where $x<-3$ and $y<2$, the slope of the slope field is negative." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725030}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "901ac968-bbda-572d-89a3-565958dd6a79" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{dy}{dx}=(-3-x)(2-y)$ and its slope field.\n\nWhich of the following statements are true? Select all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x,y)=(-3-x)(2-y)$. The slope at $(x,y)$ is $f(x,y)$. A factor is zero on $x=-3$ or $y=2$, so these are the zero-slope lines.\n\n![Zero-slope lines dividing the plane into four open regions.](images/23/23a8c43b8ec3a8a07c597730ec761f4aebc9425b4d1bd916da41ecd54e0d6560.png)\n\nAway from these lines, each factor has a fixed sign throughout each open region. Multiply the factor signs to determine the slope sign.\n\n| Region | $(-3-x)$ | $(2-y)$ | $f(x,y)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x<-3$, $y>2$ | $+$ | $-$ | $-$ |\n| $x>-3$, $y>2$ | $-$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n| $x<-3$, $y<2$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| $x>-3$, $y<2$ | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n\n![Signs of the slope in all four open regions.](images/56/56f468ed62ec56c7ad8b3f6a995ef89aa81004ddb934dc2eb7b061c3141ece30.png)\n\n- Statement 1: for $x<-3$ and $y<2$, the slope is positive. The statement is **false**.\n- Statement 2: for $x>-3$ and $y>2$, the slope is positive. The statement is **false**.\n- Statement 3: for $x>-3$ and $y<2$, the slope is negative. The statement is **false**.\n\n“None of the above” is **true** because no ordinary statement is true.\n\nThe strict inequalities exclude the zero-slope lines; the slope is zero on those lines."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725024 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10d53b9c-d3ba-503e-8312-e08762cafc31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186724976} {:answer/id #uuid "c0340820-7f07-5b81-9610-3333303fdd4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 175921