answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725054} :answer-field/id #uuid "d45cab63-6d77-5eb9-8671-9e76faa1d603" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725080}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "76fbfc73-b056-54e6-8e1c-883871565cec" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{dy}{dx}=(x+1)(y-3)$ and its slope field.\n\nThe zero-slope lines are $x=-1$ and $y=3$. Use the signs of the two factors in each region.\n\n![Zero-slope lines dividing the plane into four open regions.](images/cd/cdf7e728b9e1c09ed0f518104a7da4291858a57e161da8e892644f391498a2c4.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true? Select all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x,y)=(x+1)(y-3)$. The slope at $(x,y)$ is $f(x,y)$. A factor is zero on $x=-1$ or $y=3$, so these are the zero-slope lines.\n\n![Zero-slope lines dividing the plane into four open regions.](images/cd/cdf7e728b9e1c09ed0f518104a7da4291858a57e161da8e892644f391498a2c4.png)\n\nAway from these lines, each factor has a fixed sign throughout each open region. Multiply the factor signs to determine the slope sign.\n\n| Region | $(x+1)$ | $(y-3)$ | $f(x,y)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x<-1$, $y>3$ | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n| $x>-1$, $y>3$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| $x<-1$, $y<3$ | $-$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n| $x>-1$, $y<3$ | $+$ | $-$ | $-$ |\n\n![Signs of the slope in all four open regions.](images/13/1301c5491d6575b964de477b159af1229ecec5fedc93d6c4ef16c95696e85ee1.png)\n\n- Statement 1: for $x<-1$ and $y>3$, the slope is negative. The statement is **true**.\n- Statement 2: for $x<-1$ and $y<3$, the slope is positive. The statement is **true**.\n- Statement 3: for $x>-1$ and $y>3$, the slope is positive. The statement is **false**.\n\n“None of the above” is **false** because at least one ordinary statement is true.\n\nThe strict inequalities exclude the zero-slope lines; the slope is zero on those lines."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725066 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "51c2b859-a54a-5d80-9549-fb18c565cf34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725053} {:answer/id #uuid "7af97656-30fa-51fd-96be-edb9b3330a7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725063}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "51c2b859-a54a-5d80-9549-fb18c565cf34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725053} :answer-field/id #uuid "6b62b470-cd87-5725-86a2-2fe0b2a2d6be" :answer-field/key "At every point $(x,y)$ where $x>1$ and $y<1$, the slope of the slope field is positive." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725059} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "55603d15-50b5-5177-bd12-e84bda5b5cb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725055} {:answer/id #uuid "e7b0a9ef-9f8a-557a-ba4c-7e36812d5df4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725086}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e7b0a9ef-9f8a-557a-ba4c-7e36812d5df4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725086} :answer-field/id #uuid "7cfa4b7e-9cc9-5a96-bf67-24e4021b884d" :answer-field/key "At every point $(x,y)$ where $x>1$ and $y>1$, the slope of the slope field is negative." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725065} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ad03ecb7-be84-567d-b8c2-70ad7cdf794f" :answer/type 