ges/74/745e177822c44ab22b2c7e8c42e66c92dc3fccc6566240f3353546be518d2f2c.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true? Select all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x,y)=(x-1)(y-1)$. The slope at $(x,y)$ is $f(x,y)$. A factor is zero on $x=1$ or $y=1$, so these are the zero-slope lines.\n\n![Zero-slope lines dividing the plane into four open regions.](images/74/745e177822c44ab22b2c7e8c42e66c92dc3fccc6566240f3353546be518d2f2c.png)\n\nAway from these lines, each factor has a fixed sign throughout each open region. Multiply the factor signs to determine the slope sign.\n\n| Region | $(x-1)$ | $(y-1)$ | $f(x,y)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x<1$, $y>1$ | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n| $x>1$, $y>1$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| $x<1$, $y<1$ | $-$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n| $x>1$, $y<1$ | $+$ | $-$ | $-$ |\n\n![Signs of the slope in all four open regions.](images/a1/a1f41a19cb0f5fcecbfe19a5aedacea5bd9faa0301bcac10fea09c9d11960bde.png)\n\n- Statement 1: for $x>1$ and $y<1$, the slope is negative. The statement is **false**.\n- Statement 2: for $x>1$ and $y>1$, the slope is positive. The statement is **false**.\n- Statement 3: for $x<1$ and $y>1$, the slope is negative. The statement is **false**.\n\n“None of the above” is **true** because no ordinary statement is true.\n\nThe strict inequalities exclude the zero-slope lines; the slope is zero on those lines."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725068 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6e7e29ee-3a8f-5a3d-aa91-b481c661c422" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725060} {:answer/id #uuid "cbf5a2ed-30b3-5bf3-a6f6-e655c3bfd985" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725079}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6e7e29ee-3a8f-5a3d-aa91-b481c661c422" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db