 "e3990b84-dd64-5518-ab41-ee2ba2008501" :answer-field/key "At every point $(x,y)$ where $x>-1$ and $y>2$, the slope of the slope field is positive." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725084}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "f62a4d68-d9c3-5207-86bf-81d9f5bff112" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{dy}{dx}=(x+1)(y-2)$ and its slope field.\n\nThe zero-slope lines are $x=-1$ and $y=2$. Use the signs of the two factors in each region.\n\n![Zero-slope lines dividing the plane into four open regions.](images/73/73467ae29cc016ad0945a516c2873873ac5b961ec788a86f81e4b9f72547b21e.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true? Select all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x,y)=(x+1)(y-2)$. The slope at $(x,y)$ is $f(x,y)$. A factor is zero on $x=-1$ or $y=2$, so these are the zero-slope lines.\n\n![Zero-slope lines dividing the plane into four open regions.](images/73/73467ae29cc016ad0945a516c2873873ac5b961ec788a86f81e4b9f72547b21e.png)\n\nAway from these lines, each factor has a fixed sign throughout each open region. Multiply the factor signs to determine the slope sign.\n\n| Region | $(x+1)$ | $(y-2)$ | $f(x,y)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x<-1$, $y>2$ | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n| $x>-1$, $y>2$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| $x<-1$, $y<2$ | $-$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n| $x>-1$, $y<2$ | $+$ | $-$ | $-$ |\n\n![Signs of the slope in all four open regions.](images/db/db44e6ce36e24947d0f56e6c7b542d98400dac68ac9af70566b68774aeb0fa79.png)\n\n- Statement 1: for $x>-1$ and $y<2$, the slope is negative. The statement is **false**.\n- Statement 2: for $x<-1$ and $y>2$, the slope is negative. The statement is **true**.\n- Statement 3: for $x>-1$ and $y>2$, the slope is positive. The statement is **true**.\n\n“None of the above” is **false** because at least one ordinary statement is true.\n\nThe strict inequalities exclude the zero-slope lines; the slope is zero on those lines."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725095 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "907bb4f9-7f2b-565c-bd3b-09ea29e5df58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725098} {:answer/id #uuid "b286ef6e-09ec-5b5a-aa1f-5058be84d2c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725101}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b286ef6e-09ec-5b5a-aa1f-5058be84d2c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725101} :answer-field/id #uuid "11ed0b62-0c9c-5117-bcd6-3c874ee8245e" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725091} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "48f74026-e99c-529f-93ae-771a11979f0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725092} {:answer/id #uuid "ffc0fd2d-b8e7-5850-81bb-7b66d0121646" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725103}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "48f74026-e99c-529f-93ae-771a11979f0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725092} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a272d30-9284-50d9-a78f-bc01a3d1a5a0" :answer-field/key "At every point $(x,y)$ where $x<1$ and $y>2$, the slope of the slope field is positive." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725093} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8314e29a-1711-5cea-ad44-b2428134a37f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725097} {:answer/id #uuid "e8001e10-95b5-51b1-99de-9b7699e4910b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725102}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8314e29a-1711-5cea-ad44-b2428134a37f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725097} :answer-field/id #uuid "513ae456-df61-508f-9aef-4c4b66f3ae19" :answer-field/key "At every point $(x,y)$ where $x>1$ and $y<2$, the slope of the slope field is positive." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725094} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9bd671ca-f43e-5d6c-8eb6-ba410ae24eaa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725099} {:answer/id #uuid "aab0629b-20ea-57ae-ae06-d53b7bdd1955" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725100}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9bd671ca-f43e-5d6c-8eb6-ba410ae24eaa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725099} :answer-field/id #uuid "6eabf2f6-c6c7-5c1c-82df-1cfcab72b0e6" :answer-field/key "At every point $(x,y)$ where $x<1$ and $y<2$, the slope of the slope field is negative." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725096}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "615e614f-635a-5bed-a6e5-f4a05a37638f" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{dy}{dx}=(1-x)(y-2)^{2}$ and its slope field.\n\nWhich of the following statements are true? Select all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x,y)=(1-x)(y-2)^{2}$. The slope at $(x,y)$ is $f(x,y)$. A factor is zero on $x=1$ or $y=2$, so these are the zero-slope lines.\n\n![Zero-slope lines dividing the plane into four open regions.](images/fc/fc16b1876053de0deeaa0c5d085a13975ca2883ad29bffc764cc7e4fc2064d9a.png)\n\nAway from these lines, each factor has a fixed sign throughout each open region. Multiply the factor signs to determine the slope sign. The squared factor is strictly positive on both sides of $y=2$; it is zero on the line. Crossing this line does not reverse the sign.\n\n| Region | $(1-x)$ | $(y-2)^{2}$ | $f(x,y)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x<1$, $y>2$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| $x>1$, $y>2$ | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n| $x<1$, $y<2$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| $x>1$, $y<2$ | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n\n![Signs of the slope in all four open regions.](images/64/646e6b1237fb596521d8c6f0ec5e8df7027d238191021a1f7095726c0f080a99.png)\n\n- Statement 1: for $x<1$ and $y>2$, the slope is positive. The statement is **true**.\n- Statement 2: for $x<1$ and $y<2$, the slope is positive. The statement is **false**.\n- Statement 3: for $x>1$ and $y<2$, the slope is negative. The statement is **false**.\n\n“None of the above” is **false** because at least one ordinary statement is true.\n\nThe strict inequalities exclude the zero-slope lines; the slope is zero on those lines."}]}
